{
  "_comment": "Live config. Put your best model on unify - it writes the book. The editor must be a different model from unify, or it will approve its own work. A role's value can be a single {provider, model, ...} dict, or a LIST of them - a fallback chain tried in preference order, falling back only once a candidate's own internal retries are exhausted (see providers.call_model). Useful when one provider has a bad night: list your best model first, a more available one next, then a wholly different provider as a last resort. Pin '-latest'-style aliases where a provider offers them (e.g. mistral-small-latest) rather than a dated snapshot - it costs nothing and avoids the exact version-churn problem that broke several pinned models in this project's own history.",

